WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:06.609
Workday watches your timecard for mistakes, and sends an alert when something looks off.

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:08.661
When it does, act on it right away.

00:00:10.011 --> 00:00:10.998
First, overlap.

00:00:10.998 --> 00:00:18.106
You booked time off after your timecard filled in, so the same day now holds both hours worked and time off.

00:00:18.106 --> 00:00:22.121
Policy does not allow overlapping records, so reconcile them.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:24.688
Better still, book time off in advance.

00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:27.423
Second, daily total.

00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:31.233
Say you logged 4 hours of time off and 6 hours of work.

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:33.519
That is 10, over your 8-hour day.

00:00:33.519 --> 00:00:37.537
Your worked hours are a fact, so reduce the time off to 2.

00:00:38.887 --> 00:00:39.868
Third, on-call.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:46.865
If you are on-call eligible, do not record both on-call hours worked and on-call standby for the same week.

00:00:48.215 --> 00:00:49.469
Last, missing time.

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:53.229
Part-time employees and interns create their own entries.

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:58.242
If you get a missing time reminder, log in and submit your hours right away.
